<page type="text" lines="ocr">
  <layout>One column of verse, set left of centre, with a signature mark centred below the last line and a catchword at the lower right.</layout>
  <running_head />
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Pu-</catchword>
    <signature>II I 2 [?]</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Quos musca cum proboscide, atque vexato</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2" para="true">
      <i>Quaestus juvat labore nodus in scirpo.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3" para="true">
      <i>Sacrario isthoc masculā illa creatos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4" para="true">
      <i>Se venditat Sapientia ofa Doctores,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5" para="true">
      <i>Caelestis illa, tota quanta divina,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6" para="true">
      <i>Nihil profani noxiique contrectans,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7" para="true">
      <i>Non insolens, non aucupans novos sensus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8" para="true">
      <i>Lascivientis seculi &amp; senescentis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9" para="true">
      <i>Funestius dubium an frequentius crimen;</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10" para="true">
      <i>At strenuum illud integrans sine ampullis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11" para="true">
      <i>Lenocinantibusque inanis Verum,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12" para="true">
      <i>Quod cade signatum Dei Redemtoris,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13" para="true">
      <i>Crucibus, quadrigis, eculeisque fundatum,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14" para="true">
      <i>Tormenta per mille atque mille per mortes</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15" para="true">
      <i>Fuso cruore Martyrum, intulit caelo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16" para="true">
      <i>Animosa virtus, sancta sed Fides terris</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17" para="true">
      <i>Regina stabili sanciit sacramento</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18" para="true">
      <i>Heu! illa avitis dum stetit titolis, felix,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19" para="true">
      <i>Pietaticultrix antequam evaporavit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20" para="true">
      <i>Aetas Parentum, quae sacris procul rixis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21" para="true">
      <i>Dissentiendi sordidoque pruritu,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22" para="true">
      <i>Non glande pasta vel rudi tamen fa[?]no,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23" para="true">
      <i>Non fece pota vel sophisticis sputis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24" para="true">
      <i>At nec malo libidinantior luxu,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25" para="true">
      <i>Sed flore lactis, sed liquore Sionis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26" para="true">
      <i>De fontibus scaturiente contenta,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27" para="true">
      <i>Sciri negata scire non nimis quaerens,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28" para="true">
      <i>Diviniores se excitabat ad curas;</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29" para="true">
      <i>Nunc exul, exspes, improbisque vah! fame[?]</i>
    </l>
    <l n="30" para="true">
      <i>Contusa colaphis, quando perdidit fractas</i>
    </l>
    <l n="31" para="true">
      <i>Circum-malorum fraude-venta Tutorum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="32" para="true">
      <i>Res sacra vires, dogmatumque nascentum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="33" para="true">
      <i>Profano aceto lota, inelegantique</i>
    </l>
    <l n="34" para="true">
      <i>Postposita pellici, &amp; pedisseque jussa</i>
    </l>
    <l n="35" para="true">
      <i>Vices obire Virgo, vilior scorto,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="36" para="true">
      <i>Vah! impotente Virgo, vidit extremum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="37" para="true">
      <i>Nefas suorum: quando pristinum Candor</i>
    </l>
    <l n="38" para="true">
      <i>Sanctumque nomen, &amp; modestus illorum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="39" para="true">
      <i>Scrutator ardor, quae silentii sacrum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="40" para="true">
      <i>Post supparum verenda providum Numen</i>
    </l>
    <l n="41" para="true">
      <i>Nec vult videri tota, tota nec condi,</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Verse without visible stanza breaks; each printed line is given as its own paragraph. The initial "Q" of lines 1 and 2 and the "Q" of line 12 are large swash capitals. Doubtful readings: "fa[?]no" (line 22, possibly fæno) and "fame[?]" (line 29, ink blot over the word end). The signature mark at the foot reads as "II I 2" and is uncertain. The catchword "Pu-" at the lower right is partly smudged.</notes>
</page>
